ed","content":[{"type":"output_text","annotations":[],"logprobs":[],"text":"**(Ⅰ)** At \\(\\theta=\\pi/6\\),\n\\[\n\\rho^2\\cos\\frac{\\pi}{3}=8\n\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad \\rho^2=16,\n\\]\nso \\(\\rho=\\pm4\\). Thus, up to interchanging \\(A,B\\), their signed-radius polar coordinates are\n\\[\nA=\\left(4,\\frac{\\pi}{6}\\right),\\qquad\nB=\\left(-4,\\frac{\\pi}{6}\\right).\n\\]\nWith nonnegative radii, \\(B=(4,7\\pi/6)\\).\n\nThis uses the full-line interpretation of \\(C_2\\) implied by the stated two intersections; if \\(\\rho\\ge0\\) and \\(\\theta=\\pi/6\\) is interpreted strictly as a ray, there is only one intersection.\n\n**(Ⅱ)** Since\n\\[\n\\rho^2\\cos2\\theta=x^2-y^2,\n\\]\n\\(C_1\\) has Cartesian equation \\(x^2-y^2=8\\). Substituting the parametrized line gives\n\\[\n\\left(2+\\frac{\\sqrt3}{2}t\\right)^2-\\left(\\frac t2\\right)^2=8\n\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad\nt^2+4\\sqrt3\\,t-8=0.\n\\]\nHence\n\\[\nt_M,t_N=-2\\sqrt3\\pm2\\sqrt5.\n\\]\nThe direction vector \\((\\sqrt3/2,1/2)\\) has unit length, so\n\\[\nMN=|t_M-t_N|=4\\sqrt5.\n\\]\n\nFinal answer: \\(A=(4,\\pi/6)\\), \\(B=(-4,\\pi/6)\\equiv(4,7\\pi/6)\\); \\(\\boxed{MN=4\\sqrt5}\\)."}],"phase":"final_answer","role":"assistant"}],"parallel_tool_calls":true,"presence_penalty":0,"previous_response_id":null,"prompt_cache_key":null,"prompt_cache_retention":"24h","reasoning":{"context":"all_turns","effort":"medium","mode":"standard","summary":null},"safety_identifier":null,"service_tier":"default","store":false,"temperature":1,"text":{"format":{"type":"text"},"verbosity":"medium"},"tool_choice":"auto","tool_usage":{"image_gen":{"input_tokens":0,"input_tokens_details":{"image_tokens":0,"text_tokens":0},"output_tokens":0,"output_tokens_details":{"image_tokens":0,"text_tokens":0},"total_tokens":0},"web_search":{"num_requests":0}},"tools":[],"top_logprobs":0,"top_p":0.98,"truncation":"disabled","usage":{"input_tokens":239,"input_tokens_details":{"cache_write_tokens":0,"cached_tokens":0},"output_tokens":58